#: ../prefs.js:120
msgid ""
"Detected folders containing gnome-shell/, plus a System default option. "
"Requires the User Themes extension."
msgstr ""

#: ../prefs.js:122
msgid ""
"This only changes the top bar and the overview (the screen you get by "
"pressing the Super/Windows key) — not the look of your actual apps."
msgstr ""

#: ../prefs.js:123
msgid ""
"It works through another extension called \"User Themes.\" Picking a name "
"here just tells User Themes which theme folder to load."
msgstr ""

#: ../prefs.js:124
msgid ""
"\"(System default)\" means \"don’t use a custom one, just use GNOME’s own "
"built-in look.\" That’s also why you won’t see \"Adwaita\" as a pickable "
"name here even though it’s the default — it’s built in, not a folder on disk "
"like other themes are, so pick \"(System default)\" instead when you want it."
msgstr ""

#: ../prefs.js:125
msgid ""
"If nothing happens when this switches, make sure the \"User Themes\" "
"extension is installed and turned on."
msgstr ""

